// Ported slice (part 3) of the source-driven CompilerPipelineOptimizeSsaTests.cs
// optimization / value-fact tests, running against the current C# host compiler
// through the host test protocol. Each Impl compiles the embedded Stark program
// (kept verbatim from the C# raw string) through the closest compile helper and
// returns a bool.
//
// PORT-NOTE (suite-wide): the original C# tests inspect the structured
// SsaIrModule / SsaValueFactModel object model (block instructions, RValue
// subtypes, per-value integer-range / known-bits / nullability / length facts,
// block entry/exit fact tables, pass logs, etc.). The host source-in /
// rendered-artifact-text-out bridge cannot reconstruct those typed inputs, so
// each ported assertion is reduced to the nearest text/Succeeds signal over the
// rendered `ssa` (post-named-pass) artifact. Per-method PORT-NOTE comments name
// what was reduced where it is not obvious. The C# tests remain the oracle until
// cutover.

